panel-simple: undo loader protection when the loader route fails

rockchip_drm's setup_initial_state() calls loader_protect(on) on the panel
before it knows whether the bootloader actually left a display running, and
panel_simple_loader_protect(on) marks the panel prepared and enabled without
touching hardware. When the route then fails -- on the TAQ-102 U-Boot never
brings the LVDS panel up, so the kernel logs "can't not find any loader
display" -- the error path calls loader_protect(off), whose body was
"/* do nothing */". The flags stay set, the first real prepare() returns
early, and the enable GPIO stays wherever U-Boot parked it: measured
output-low on this board, with a 50 ms register poll showing no transition
through the modeset. Only a later unprepare/prepare cycle (glcube exiting
and restarting) ever raised it, which is why a second modeset showed the
picture and the first did not.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-simple.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-simple.c
@@ -561,7 +561,14 @@ static int panel_simple_loader_protect(struct drm_panel *panel, bool on)
 		p->prepared = true;
 		p->enabled = true;
 	} else {
-		/* do nothing */
+		/*
+		 * The loader did not leave this panel running after all, so
+		 * undo what the on path assumed; otherwise prepare() sees
+		 * prepared == true and never drives the enable GPIO.
+		 */
+		panel_simple_regulator_disable(panel);
+		p->prepared = false;
+		p->enabled = false;
 	}

 	return 0;
